meta {
  name: Lookup Mailer (Not Found)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/mailers/NOSUCHQCN123
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 404 Not Found", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(404);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /mailers/:controlNumber — unknown number

  A miss is a **404**, and in the drawer it is an ordinary outcome rather than
  an error: a producer half-way through typing a control number has not made a
  mistake. The web client catches this status in `lib/mailers-api.ts` and
  returns `null`, so the drawer renders its "no record" empty state from a
  successful query rather than an error state — and TanStack Query never treats
  the miss as retryable.

  The same 404, with the same body, covers three cases on purpose: no mailer
  carries that number, the input normalized to nothing (`---`), and the mailer
  belongs to a different agency. Distinguishing them would disclose whether
  another tenant holds the record.
}
